      "text": "To solve the given problem, we need to find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) of \\( f(x) = 16x + 3 \\), and then solve the equation \\( f^{-1}(x) = f((2x)^{-1}) \\).\n\n1. **Finding the Inverse Function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\):**\n   - Start with the function \\( y = f(x) = 16x + 3 \\).\n   - Solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n     \\[\n     y = 16x + 3\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     y - 3 = 16x\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{y - 3}{16}\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, the inverse function is:\n     \\[\n     f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 3}{16}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Substituting into the Main Equation:**\n   - We have given the equation \\( f^{-1}(x) = f\\left(\\left(2x\\right)^{-1}\\right) \\).\n   - Substitute \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) and \\( f\\left(\\left(2x\\right)^{-1}\\right) \\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{x - 3}{16} = f\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Now, compute \\( f\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)\\right) \\):\n     \\[\n     f\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)\\right) = 16 \\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) + 3 = \\frac{16}{2x} + 3 = \\frac{8}{x} + 3\n     \\]\n   - So the equation becomes:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{x - 3}{16} = \\frac{8}{x} + 3\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solving the Equation:**\n   - Multiply both sides by 16 to eliminate the denominator on the left:\n     \\[\n     x - 3 = 16\\left(\\frac{8}{x} + 3\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Simplify the right side:\n     \\[\n     x - 3 = \\frac{128}{x} + 48\n     \\]\n   - Move all terms to one side of the equation:\n     \\[\n     x - 3 - \\frac{128}{x} - 48 = 0\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     x - \\frac{128}{x} - 51 = 0\n     \\]\n   - Multiply through by \\( x \\) to clear the fraction:\n     \\[\n     x^2 - 128 - 51x = 0\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     x^2 - 51x - 128 = 0\n     \\]\n\n4. **Solving the Quadratic Equation:**\n   - Use the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\) where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = -51 \\), and \\( c = -128 \\):\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{-(-51) \\pm \\sqrt{(-51)^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-128)}}{2 \\cdot 1}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{51 \\pm \\sqrt{2601 + 512}}{2}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{51 \\pm \\sqrt{3113}}{2}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Summing the Solutions:**\n   - The quadratic equation has two solutions:\n     \\[\n     x_1 = \\frac{51 + \\sqrt{3113}}{2}, \\quad x_2 = \\frac{51 - \\sqrt{3113}}{2}\n     \\]\n   - The sum of the solutions to a quadratic equation \\( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \\) is given by \\( -\\frac{b}{a} \\):\n     \\[\n     x_1 + x_2 = -\\frac{-51}{1} = 51\n     \\]\n\nThus, the sum of all \\( x \\) that satisfy the given equation is \\(\\boxed{51}\\).",
